-- Tests for pc-body-b-deferred-images.l4: Penal Code 1871, Chapter 16, ss 377BB to
-- 377BO and 377C, completed in the pass of 2026-11-04.
--
-- Where the expected values come from.
--
-- * The structural cases (the first part) are generated by
--   generators/deferred/gen_struct_tests.py from the elements each section's
--   spec lists (written from the Code's words) and, for the definitions, the
--   rules of reading and the defences, from the shape the text gives each:
--   "means" and "if" give JUST TRUE where the condition holds and JUST FALSE
--   where it does not; "includes" and a grant limited by its own wording give
--   JUST TRUE where it holds and NOTHING where it does not; "it is not
--   necessary" and "it is not a defence" give JUST FALSE whatever the input.
--   For each offence: a set of facts meeting every element (one per
--   alternative of an "or"), one set per element with that element alone made
--   untrue, and a set with nothing established.  Nothing is read from output.
--   What they test is that the L4 says what the spec says; they cannot find a
--   spec that misreads the text.
-- * The cases written by hand (the second part) are the Code's own
--   Illustrations (cited above each: s 377BE(5), 377C(3)(f), 377BK(3),
--   377BM(2), 377BN(3), 377BN(4), 377BO), the presumption of s 377BB(9),
--   s 377C(3)(c), and the offence defined over another offence's facts
--   (s 377BO).
-- * A failing assertion is a finding.  None has been edited to match the code.
-- By one Sonnet 5.5 agent, 2026-11-04.  The text is the converter's plain-text rendering of Singapore Statutes Online ("Current version as at 09 Sep 2026"), not the official text.

